<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26878" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŏcālis</span></b> , e,
			adj.
		locus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a place, local</i>
			(late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">determinatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 4, 34</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">locale universali opponit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ad Scapul. 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aerumnae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 14, 7, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adverbia,</span>”
				<i>adverbs of place</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Charis. p. 182</span></i>
			 P.—Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŏcālĭter</span></b> , <i>locally</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Besae dei localiter appellati oraculum,</span>”
				i. e. <i>by the inhabitants</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 19, 12, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Tert. Pall. 2</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Cassiod. Var. 1, 35</span></i>.</div>
